      "title": "13 \u00b7 Krea 2 depth",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 14 \u00b7 Z-Image Union ControlNet\n\nThe only Z-Image ControlNet running in MLX. Holds the geometry of a source image while the prompt\ndecides everything else: medium, palette, lighting, materials.\n\n**How the control image is read:** the preprocessor runs locally, so you feed the ORIGINAL photo,\nnot a pre-computed edge map. `control_type` says how to read it: `canny`, `depth`, `hed`, `mlsd`\nor `pose`.\n\n**Stacking:** chain a second `mflux Image` and set `control_type` to a comma-separated list in the\nsame order, e.g. `canny,depth`. Each control keeps its own strength, taken from that node's\n`strength` widget.\n\n**Things that silently go wrong:**\n- One `control_type` for several images is fine (it applies to all). A list whose length does not\n  match the number of chained images is an error, on purpose, rather than a silent mispairing.\n- Feed the photo on `image`, not on `map_image`. The ControlNet computes its own map.\n- Strength lives on each `mflux Image` (0.6-0.8 is a good start). Too high and the prompt cannot\n  change the medium; too low and the composition drifts.\n- Z-Image Turbo is distilled: leave `guidance` at 0 and `steps` at 8."
      ],
      "color": "#2a363b",
      "bgcolor": "#1e2a30"
    },
